! jb_af1c F217 "DIVIDE TEST ROUTINE", sub-block F217B "TESTS OF SIGN
! AND MODIFIER COMBINATIONS", p.155 (octal 020666.40-020703.00).
! Continues fp_arith_f217a.strap; F217C follows immediately at
! 020703.40, which is why this block has no exit branch of its own.
!
! The listing's header names the axes: "MS+MEM. SIGN, ACS+ACC. SIGN, N
! AND A ARE MODIFIERS".  Four rows, each checking one bit -- the
! quotient sign in sign byte bit 4.  p.93: "The quotient sign replaces
! the accumulator sign in bit position 4 of the sign byte register",
! and the sign is "determined by the rules of algebra using the
! accumulator sign and the effective sign of the addressed operand".
!
!   B1  LN FPK64 (acc sign 1) / FPK52 (0)       -> 1   BB
!   B2  L  FPK64 (acc sign 0) / FPK55 (1)       -> 1   BB
!   B3  LN FPK64 (acc sign 1) / FPK55 (1)       -> 0   BZB
!   B4  LN FPK64 (acc sign 1) / NA FPK55        -> 0   BZB
!
! THE POOL IS BUILT FOR THIS.  FPK52 and FPK55 are the same number but
! for bit 3, and so are FPK64 and FPK69 -- the constants come in
! sign-pairs so a block like this can vary one axis at a time.  It is
! also what makes FPK64 easy to mis-transcribe as FPK69: they differ in
! that one bit and sit next to each other in the pool.
!
! B4 IS THE ONLY ROW WITH A MODIFIER, and its A is invisible: FPK55's
! sign is already 1, so absolute-then-negate gives 1 just as negate
! alone would.  B4 and B3 therefore expect the same answer and differ
! only in the modifier bits the instruction carries.  That is the
! recurring shape -- a modifier that forces a sign positive cannot be
! seen where the sign is already what it would become -- and it means
! the A modifier is untested by F217 unless B3/B4 are read as a pair
! against an implementation that ignores N as well.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes: SERS (octal 1304) -> FAIL halt,
! -- SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch.
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool pp.176-177) --
        SLC, (8)22071.0
FPK52   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001024713560247135620
        SLC, (8)22074.0
FPK55   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001024713560247135630
        SLC, (8)22104.0
FPK64   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001051627340516273440

        SLC, (8)20666.40
! F217B1 - MS 0, N+A 0, ACS 1
F217B   LN(U), FPK64
        /(U), FPK52
        BB, $SB+.4, $+2.0                    ! test sign bit + 1
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
! F217B2 - MS 1, ACS+N+A 0
ROD1    L(U), FPK64
        /(U), FPK55
        BB, $SB+.4, $+2.0                    ! test sign bit + 1
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
! F217B3 - MS+ACS 1, N+A 0
        B, $+.32
ROD2    LN(U), FPK64
        /(U), FPK55
        BZB, $SB+.4, $+2.0                   ! test sign bit + 0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
! F217B4 - MS+ACS+N+A 1
        B, $+.32
ROD3    LN(U), FPK64
        /NA(U), FPK55
        BZB, $SB+.4, $+2.0                   ! test sign bit + 0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                               ! 020703.40: F217C's first instruction
        END, F217B
